# Stage

Brand new app, no users, no data worth keeping.

- **Local is disposable.** The dev database and `./data-pg` get blown away and
  regenerated. Never design around preserving them, never hedge about losing
  them, never propose a migration path for local data.
- **No back-compat.** Nothing is deployed to users yet. Prefer deleting and
  rewriting over a compatibility shim. One-time destructive fixes are fine —
  drop the database, recreate the bucket, rewrite the schema.
- **Optimize for change management, not first-time setup.** A rough one-time
  step is fine. Anything repeated weekly should be one command that's hard to
  get wrong. Spend the effort on the second.

Corollary: don't build guards against mistakes I'd only make once during
setup. Do build them for anything on the deploy path.
